// Custom local-table migration: game_backlog.
//
// Table game_backlog holds the user's personal game backlog — one row per
// RAWG game id, mirroring the rawg_id/title/slug identity used by the live
// commands and adding local play-tracking state that RAWG does not model:
//   - status      backlog | in-progress | finished | dropped
//   - hours       hours played (local, RAWG has no per-user playtime)
//   - added_at    RFC3339 UTC timestamp when the row was first added
//                 (never rewritten by upserts — the age drives the queue's
//                 longest-waiting tier and the already-present notice)
//   - finished_at RFC3339 UTC set when status first flips to finished,
//                 cleared when the row leaves finished
//   - user_rating RAWG-style 1-5 rating the user assigns after finishing
//   - notes       free-form local notes
//
// Migration is idempotent (CREATE TABLE/INDEX IF NOT EXISTS) and runs from
// migrateExtras, so every read-write store open converges to the same schema.

